{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.MagnitudeTraceCommutator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.MagnitudeTraceCommutator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.trace_comp_conjOp_sub_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.trace_comp_conjOp_sub_id","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/MagnitudeTraceCommutator.lean#L86-L97","doc":"**The operator lemma `M ∘ (Q − 1) = 0` (sorry-free).**  The commutator\ndefect `[Q, M]` is annihilated by `M`: `trace ∘ (conjOp u − id) = 0` as\nlinear maps `End V → R` — the operator form of `tr_M([Q, M]) = 0`, and the\nreason no trace-based (class-function) functional, including the surreal\nbirthday of `tr_M`, separates conjugate operators.  Crossing the wall\nrequires a functional nonzero on the commutator subspace `[H, H]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.trace_comp_conjOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.trace_comp_conjOp","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/MagnitudeTraceCommutator.lean#L75-L83","doc":"**The operator lemma `M ∘ Q = M` (sorry-free).**  As linear maps\n`End V → R`, the magnitude `M = trace` composed with the conjugation\n`Q`-step `conjOp u` equals `M`: the quantifier step is invisible to the\nmagnitude functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.conjOp_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.conjOp_apply","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/MagnitudeTraceCommutator.lean#L71-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.conjOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.conjOp","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/MagnitudeTraceCommutator.lean#L63-L68","doc":"The **quantifier `Q`-step as an operator**: conjugation by a unit `u`, an\nR-linear map on `End V` (relabel the computation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.magnitude_trace_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.magnitude_trace_conj","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/MagnitudeTraceCommutator.lean#L57-L61","doc":"**Magnitude is conjugation-invariant (sorry-free): `tr(u f u⁻¹) = tr f`.**\nThe scalar form of `M ∘ Q = M` — Markov move I for the Jones invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.magnitude_trace_commutator_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.magnitude_trace_commutator_zero","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/MagnitudeTraceCommutator.lean#L48-L54","doc":"**`M` kills the commutator `[Q, M]` (sorry-free): `tr([f, g]) = 0`.**  The\nmagnitude functional (a trace) is blind to the commutator defect — `QM` and\n`MQ` carry equal magnitude.  Toda-blindness realized by the categorical\ntrace. ","signatureChunk":0}]}